I ran `git blame` on all 18 tracked files, which covers 1,995 lines. I used `-w -M -C` so whitespace changes and moved or copied lines don't take ownership from the original author.

The latest commit, `62628c0` ("reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes"), rewrote about 1,000 lines. Blamed naively, it gives its author, Fiona Formatter, 291 lines, which is third place. That is only a reformat, not authorship. The table below skips that commit with `--ignore-rev 62628c0`, so each line goes to whoever last changed it in substance.

