FINAL ANSWER:
**Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson own most of the code that's still here, roughly 40% and 32% of the lines. A naive blame says otherwise.**

**Why the naive result is wrong:** The latest commit, `62628c0`, was a mechanical reformat to 4-space indent and double quotes. It was authored by "Fiona Formatter", who has no other commits. A plain blame gives that commit about 51% of all lines, including 94% of `test/test.js` and 90% of `lib/index.js`. That ownership is only whitespace and quote changes, so I discarded it.

**How I measured it:** I ran `git blame -w -M -C --ignore-rev 62628c0` over every tracked file, which credits each line to whoever last changed its substance. These are line counts across about 1,950 lines.

| Author | Surviving lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 810 | ~41% |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 629 | ~32% |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 95 | ~5% |
| Jon Church | 72 | ~4% |
| Sebastian Beltran | 67 | ~3% |
| Ulises Gascón | 52 | ~3% |
| Ignacio Mangas | 44 | ~2% |
| Everyone else (~25 people) | the remainder | ~10% |

**What each of them owns:**
- **Troy Goode:** Most of `lib/index.js` and the tests (`test/test.js`, `test/vary.js`, `test/issue-2.js`, `test/error-response.js`, `test/example-app.js`), plus a large part of the README.
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson:** `HISTORY.md`, `LICENSE`, `.eslintrc.yml`, much of `package.json`, and the largest share of `ci.yml`. His last commit was in 2021, so this is mostly repo scaffolding.
- **The `.github` workflows:** Íñigo Marquínez Prado owns `scorecard.yml`, Sebastian Beltran owns `codeql.yml`, and Ulises Gascón owns `dependabot.yml`.

**Caveats:**
- The ignore-rev blame credits a line to its last real change. Where the reformat only rewrapped a line, the original author keeps credit. Where it merged or split lines, `-w` and `-M` handle most cases but not all, so treat the percentages as approximate.
- The knowledge-risk tool counts everyone as inactive because I left its cutoff at 6 months ago and the most recent activity is April 2026. By that measure all 18 files are "orphaned", and I wouldn't read much into that.
- I did not check how the code is licensed or who holds the copyright. Line ownership here means authorship, and `LICENSE` is the place to look for legal ownership.

